      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T02:58:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This is not correct. The Normal shall only be logged when all the\n\u003e threshold assertions have been cleared.\n\nAgreed, that is the behavior I want to fix. Before the patch 51 only\nconsiders the logged thresholds, so it doesn\u0027t follow this rule when a\nthreshold has `Log` disabled.\n\n\u003e Can\u0027t you rely on Dbus interfaces to figure this out ?\n\nYes. The Asserted property of xyz.openbmc_project.Common.Threshold is\nalready maintained by HealthMetric for every threshold, regardless of\n`Log`. I already use it instead of tracking the assertion state separately:\nwhen a threshold is deasserted and Asserted becomes empty, the normal\nevent is logged (only if an assertion event was logged before). This\ncheck will be done in HealthMetric::checkThreshold() for every deassert,\nso it also works when the last threshold to clear has `Log` disabled.",
      "revId": "2d2304fb23151e5ddc3bd30fa94fd2ec5184e451",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
